  "body": "Follow-up from #17. After #17 the motion debug blade links 34 / 51 times (swarf / advanced). Holding the pose on the raster's exit rise reached 23, but the app verifier read that posed feed in air as a blocking Envelope warning (14.8 mm rest) in swarf_generates_blade_lying_axes_and_verifies_clean and advanced_swarf_adds_the_coarse_rungs, so the in-air hold was withdrawn.\n\nDone means either: the exit rise becomes a rapid, or the posed contact law excuses a feed that leaves along the surface normal, with the link ratchets in swarf_pose_continuity.rs lowered and both app tests still verifying clean.\n\nSource: RECOMMENDED.md #17 entry (owed).",
